From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spec : add adaptive MTP draft depth (draft-mtp-adaptive)

Upstream PR ggml-org/llama.cpp#27210 (head c1c2b286f9, author Stew Forster, MIT),
rebased onto b12207 (998200491327347eed85f007e4de7a1a7c871453). New speculative type
`draft-mtp-adaptive`: the MTP draft depth climbs and drops with the acceptance rate;
`--spec-draft-n-min-adaptive` is the floor, `--spec-draft-n-max` the ceiling.
The plain `draft-mtp` type is unchanged.

Changes from the PR diff when rebased onto b12207 (patch 0110, moe-cache):
- src/models/delta-net-base.cpp hunk DROPPED: b12207 already writes only the last
  min(n_seq_tokens, K) conv-state snapshots (llm_graph_context::build_conv_state_store,
  Kw = min(n, K)), which is what that hunk did on the older code. The target graph is
  therefore untouched by this patch.
- common/common.cpp: the `spec_mtp` line is written at 4 spaces in b12207 (8 in the PR base);
  same one-line change to has_mtp().
- common/speculative.cpp: two hunks re-placed by hand (n_max_user before the llm layer-cap
  block; the accept_partial override after accept() of the MTP impl).
- tests/CMakeLists.txt: the new test is registered next to test-arg-parser (line moved).
Nothing else differs from the PR diff.

